This project is based on breeze-tts2-ptbr-lora-training by EdnilsonMonteiro
(Apache-2.0) and has been modified:
(source: https://github.com/EdnilsonMonteiro/breeze-tts2-ptbr-lora-training,
commit 6c414bd)

- Adapted from Brazilian Portuguese to German (plus English): the package
  ptbr_lora/ is now de_lora/; German and English instruction pools selected by
  the corpus-name suffix (_de / _en); number expansion (num2words) selected by
  the same suffix; German probe sentences plus English/Chinese regression
  probes for the audio samples, with a per-language WER check.
- New corpus builders: CML-TTS German (referenced through a symlink, no copy),
  HUI-Audio-Corpus-German (SNR and mains-hum filtering) and HiFiTTS-2 (English).
- A consolidated codec-code store (one int16 stream plus an index) replaces the
  per-utterance .npz files and the wavs24/ copies.
- The parity check uses gold examples from all corpora (the template only used
  its "tata" corpus and therefore checked nothing for other corpora).
- Fixed the seconds-per-step value in the training log (it was divided by
  grad_acc twice).
- Rare-word tooling: word lists from wordfreq, tokenizer coverage and
  espeak-ng stress; mining of clips with rare words in Thorsten-Voice, CML-TTS
  and Common Voice; restoring the capitalization of lowercase transcripts; a
  per-clip rare-word re-weighting of the training sampler.
- A broad Common Voice selection capped per speaker, and corpus weights.
- Noise-augmented reference prompts with a "clean studio recording" instruction.
- Scripts for merging a LoRA and converting it to GGUF, run recipes, ROCm
  (MIOpen) setup, configuration through environment variables, and English
  documentation; comments and messages were translated to English.
- docker/Dockerfile now installs requirements-engine.txt (the engine's former
  requirements.txt); requirements.txt lists the training dependencies.

